---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Hotel Menu Guide"
  description="Privacy policy for Hotel Menu Guide: what cookies we use (analytics and advertising, with your consent), what we collect, and your choices."
  path="/privacy-policy/"
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-soft">Last updated: October 12, 2026</p>

    <div class="prose-guide mt-6">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        This site has no accounts and no forms that store your data. We do use
        <strong>Google Analytics</strong> to understand visits in aggregate, and we plan to
        show <strong>Google AdSense</strong> advertising. Both use cookies — but only if you
        click <strong>Accept</strong> on the cookie banner. Click <strong>Reject</strong> and
        we store nothing beyond your choice itself.
      </p>
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        We don't ask for your name, email, or any personal information anywhere on this
        site. If you accept cookies, Google's services (Analytics and AdSense) may collect
        technical data such as pages visited, approximate location, device and browser type —
        handled under <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Privacy Policy</a>,
        not ours. The contact page links to public social profiles; if you message us there,
        that conversation lives on that platform under its own privacy policy.
      </p>
      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        When you first visit, a banner asks you to <strong>Accept</strong> or
        <strong>Reject</strong> cookies:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Accept:</strong> allows Google Analytics cookies (to measure visits) and Google advertising cookies (for AdSense ads, which may be personalised).</li>
        <li><strong>Reject:</strong> blocks analytics and advertising storage. We still remember your choice itself (in your browser's local storage) so we don't ask again.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You can change your mind any time with the <strong>Cookie Settings</strong> link in
        the site footer, which re-opens the banner.
      </p>
      <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
      <p>
        We use <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> (measurement ID G-VF47V2VLCW) with Google's
        Consent Mode: no analytics data is sent until you accept. We are preparing to serve
        <strong>Google AdSense</strong> ads (see our <a href="/ads.txt">ads.txt</a>); ad
        personalisation also waits for your acceptance. Rejecting means you may still see
        ads, but they won't be personalised to you.
      </p>
      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        Our guides link to restaurants' official websites and public profiles. Once you follow one
        of those links, their privacy policies apply, not ours.
      </p>
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy ever changes, we'll update the date above.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
